WEBVTT

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.770
<b>Chihayafuru</b>

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.400
Th-Thank you...

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.060
Thank you for playing karuta with me!

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.300
Chihaya, Taichi...

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.150
But I doubt we'll ever 
see each other again.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.910
Why?

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.000
As long as we have karuta,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.930
we'll see each other again, right?

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.830
As long as we keep playing, 
we'll see each other again!

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.250
I just know it!

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.070
Verse 1

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.070
May 
it be 
that
 I find

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:53.030
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower
 blooms, but for winter</i>

00:00:54.490 --> 00:01:01.490
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:12.460
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.000
<b>Team 
Chihayafuru</b>

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.010
Get set!

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.930
Did you see that start?

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.480
Is she really a beginner at this?

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.600
That was amazing, Ayase-san!

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.230
You got off to a flying start!

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.480
Thanks!

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.230
You should really join the track team!

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.320
But then I'd have less time
to play karuta...

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.620
Oh, but that start felt 
just like playing karuta!

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.580
Just like leaping forward
the moment a card is read!

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.750
<b>Fuchu City Katamachi Cultural Center</b>

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.500
Dr. Harada! I brought a friend!

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.250
Ah! Welcome!

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.420
This is my friend from the track team,
Horikawa Michiru-chan.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.800
It's nice to meet you.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.010
Nice to meet you.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.720
Wait... Chihaya-chan,
you joined the track team?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.560
Um... Only on a trial basis, for now.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.890
I asked her to join.
Our school doesn't have a karuta club.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.600
And in exchange for joining, I asked her
to check out our karuta society.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.400
I've never played before, though.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.400
Not a problem.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.070
In competitive karuta,
the first verse of a poem is read,

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.700
and players try to take the card 
with the second verse on it.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:26.040
Today we're using practice cards that
have the unique syllables on them in red,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.790
so even if you haven't 
memorized Hundred Poets—

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.000
Um... unique syllables?

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.380
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River
 Impassionate</i>

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.880
The syllables at the start
 of the first verse

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.550
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River 
 Impassionate</i>

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.550
Ariwara no Narihira 
Impassionate gods have 
never seen the red 
that is the Tatsuta River

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.050
that help you identify which card
to take once you've heard them.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:36.340
Oh...

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.180
The deck has 100 cards,
and the players take 25 each,

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:50.100
<b><i>Opponent's Side</i></b>

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:50.100
<b><i>Player's Side</i></b>

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.180
line them up on their sides,
and put the remaining cards away.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.100
Huh? What happens to the other 50 cards?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.520
They're called "dead cards." 
They aren't used in the game.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.940
But any of the 100 cards can be read,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.900
so if a dead card is read, 
and you touch any card...

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.440
That's a fault.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.990
Then your opponent gets to 
send you one of their cards.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.280
Oh...

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.620
Oh, also, you can touch any cards
on the side with the poem that was read...

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.910
Huh? You can?

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.790
But touching any cards on 
the other side is a fault,

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.960
and you're sent a card.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.710
The first player with zero cards
left on their side wins.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:14.460
<b>Win</b>

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:14.460
<b>Lose</b>

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.960
Memorization time is over.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.090
Time to begin.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:26.180
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.300
Thank you for the game.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.600
Uh... Thank you for the game.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.560
Thank you for the game.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:33.650
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.190
Thank you very much.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.240
You're incredible, Ayase-san.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.320
I couldn't take a single card.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.160
I had a really hard time
the first time I played, too.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.370
Really?

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.240
Yep.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.870
What is with you?!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.080
You're too good!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.960
But you were able to take a card.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.130
Only one card!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.630
B-But I had fun!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.390
I wonder how Glasses is doing...

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:06.390
Huh?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.640
Eyelashes hasn't been by lately, either.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.980
I guess he's busy with 
schoolwork and club.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.520
I don't really understand karuta that well,

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.650
but I can definitely see 
how much you love it!

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.360
One more game, then!

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.110
Huh?!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.070
Er, um...

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.080
This is the place, right?

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.420
Yep, I looked it up on the internet.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.710
So Mashima's also going to play karuta?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.170
I actually have a life, so I can't 
spend all my time playing karuta,

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.340
but I'll be better than you in no time!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.550
I stole them.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.390
Don't tell Chihaya.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.400
I don't want her to hate me.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.410
Are you playing karuta with 
that scary look on your face?

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.210
When do you find it easiest 
to move around freely?

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.380
When did you have the 
most fun playing karuta?

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.180
I did it! I got a card!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.510
I beat Wataya-kun to a card!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.720
Where I was always happy, having fun,

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.180
and wishing it'd never end...

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.570
There's mine!

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.480
Mine, too!

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.070
<i>I'll find new teammates in high school</i>

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.360
<i>and devote myself 100 percent to karuta!</i>

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:55.330
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.150
Forward.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.440
We can only move forward.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.530
One...

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.820
Raise them slowly,
then lower them slowly!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.120
Two...

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.660
I can't hear you, first-years!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.660
Three...

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:19.160
<i>The Fujisaki Karuta Club is more 
athletic-minded than I thought!</i>

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.750
Some students from other schools 
have joined us for this camp.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.460
You are to practice with them proactively 
and exchange thoughts and advice.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.880
Why are you here, Retro-kun?

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.970
You'd better not interfere 
with Hokuo's secret training!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.970
Regardless of your ranks,

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.430
you'll play two matches this morning,
followed by jogging and stretches.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.180
After lunch, you'll play three matches, 
followed by jogging and stretches.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:35.890
<i>Five matches, huh?</i>

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:36.930
<i>That's pretty standard.</i>

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.180
After dinner, you will play two 
more matches in the evening.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.640
Tomorrow will consist of mountain 
climbing in the morning,

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.310
and four matches between 
morning and afternoon.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.610
Karuta is a sport of contradictions.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.360
If you take cards too fast, 
you'll commit more faults,

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.820
but if you're slow, you lose cards.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.780
Learn how to live with that contradiction.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.410
Find the point of intersection between 
contradictions that works best for you!

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.240
<i>Wow...</i>

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.790
Suffer now so that you can endure 
the toughest matches with ease!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:04.250
Those who have never felt pushed to 
the limit will never grow stronger!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.420
<i>Wow!</i>

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.590
Is practicing with your left hand
even going to help?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.630
I-It's better than no practice at all.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.640
I don't know how these Fujisaki kids
are keeping up with this.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.220
Well, it's because they respect her.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.140
Respect?

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.140
Wha?! You came here without knowing?!

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:27.520
Coach Sakurazawa never became Queen,
but she's been the runner-up five times.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.530
She was called the strongest 
challenger of all.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.320
Ba-dump!

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.280
Ba-dump?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.200
That was tough...

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.950
I never want to see a card again.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.410
This is still better than last year.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.240
Hey, Makoto-senpai was here earlier.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.790
No way! You think he's still here?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.920
It's not as if I'm here just to see you.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.000
Okay...

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.710
I only came to see
how our vice captain was doing.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:51.420
Okay...

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.010
Peanut Gallery

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.800
W-Want to go to... the beach or something?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:57.720
Huh?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.760
No, wait! That's not what I meant!

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.180
I meant with other people! Yeah!

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.060
To improve relations, even friendships, 
between club members!

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:05.640
I'll go!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.770
Yay!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.150
I'm going to the beach with Makoto-senpai!

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.360
Way to go, Yamashiro-san!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.190
<i>Relations. Friendships.</i>

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.740
Ayase-san, I bet you have a lot 
of plans for summer break, huh?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:20.740
I have club and a karuta camp at Lake Yamanaka
with the Shiranami Society. That's all.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.200
That's all?

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.660
Karuta freak

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.830
<i>She's as much of a karuta freak
as we've heard.</i>

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.710
Ayase-san, do you have a boyfriend?

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.750
You must have one!
I bet guys are all over you!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.960
Does he play karuta?

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.710
<i>Th-This is... love talk! It's love talk!</i>

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.710
<b>Love talk!!</b>

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.430
I... I don't have a boyfriend.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.720
Oh, come on! What about
the Mizusawa club president?

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:44.730
But if I don't get better at karuta,
I won't even get to sit across him,

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.480
so I have to work hard.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.610
<i>Love talk! Love talk! Love talk!</i>

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.980
Love talk!!

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.940
<i>Karuta freaks are freaks 
in all kinds of ways...</i>

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.020
Friendships

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.150
Friendships
Beach

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:51.980
Friendships
Beach
Relations

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.740
That's amazing, though. 
It's like you have a crush on karuta.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.200
If I make it to Class B in the next 
tournament, maybe I'll confess.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.780
What? To who?

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.660
Out of the second-years,
it'd have to be Hyuga, right?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.950
President Cheers?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.790
No way         No way

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.790
I'm so bummed out
that all the third-years left!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.380
But we might get to
go to the beach with them!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.840
You think Eromu-senpai will go?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.460
<b>Totally!</b>

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.460
I should've confessed when we lost to
Mizusawa at the High School Championship.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.260
I was too busy crying to even 
think about that at the time.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.050
Me, too!

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:26.930
<b>Victory for Fujisaki</b>

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.430
<i>That's how they all felt at that tournament?</i>

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.390
<i>I never knew.</i>

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:30.810
<i>Liking someone,
sharing the same feelings...</i>

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.570
<i>How did Arata feel?</i>

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.360
<i>I have no idea.</i>

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.990
<i>But I want to know.</i>

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.330
<i>I'm pretty sure I don't 
understand anything yet.</i>

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.580
Hey, Mashima-kun, why do you play karuta?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:52.540
Huh?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.840
I play to impress the ladies. Cheers!

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.840
Wh-Who are you again?

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.010
I'm Fujisaki's new club president,
Hyuga Yoshihiko.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.050
Cheers!

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.350
<i>The new president? Him?</i>

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.850
Hey, could you tell me something?

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:07.470
What is it? Ask me anything.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.560
But first... cheers!

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.090
Yeah, uh... cheers.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.730
So there's a public bath nearby? Cool!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:15.360
Huh?

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:17.400
The lights are on.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.200
President Cheers and 
Mizusawa's club president?

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.450
Like this?

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.200
Is your left hip stretching?

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.330
Wow, that's dedication.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.870
<i>Taichi's learning stretches...</i>

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.870
And so late at night...

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.500
Tsk! He really never misses 
a trick, does he?!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.200
Retro-kun!

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:33.130
He's even trying to learn Fujisaki's 
traditional physical training!

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.210
He should be more full of 
himself and slack off!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:40.470
Slack off... Slack off... Slack off...

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.470
I don't usually see you cursing 
people like that, Retro-kun.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.260
Why wouldn't I want to curse him?!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.680
He won all seven of his matches today!

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.180
Huh? He did?

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.510
Wow, Taichi's doing great!

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:51.140
Don't be too confident. 
You're in danger yourself.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:51.520
Huh?

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.850
What're you talking about, Retro-kun?

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.190
I almost always beat Taichi.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.650
You've never played him in 
an official match, have you?

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.280
Huh?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.280
This occurred to me at 
the summer tournament...

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:08.540
I think Mashima plays better 
when you're not with him.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:10.790
What?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.330
Let's call it a night.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.420
I want to commit this to muscle memory
a little more before I go.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:21.380
<i>I'm pretty sure I don't 
understand anything yet.</i>

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.390
<i>Not even about Taichi.</i>

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.810
What? Kana-chan left?!

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:31.560
Well, she lives really close to here...

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.190
That's not what training camps are about!

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.810
Tests of courage! Fireworks! Pillow fights!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:39.570
I wanted to have a sleepover with Kana-chan!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.570
Shut up, Yusei! Rub my shoulders!

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:43.200
I should've gone to Fujisaki's camp.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.620
<i>Prez, you can leave the others to me!</i>

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.200
<i>Good luck with Chihaya-chan!</i>

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.950
<i>It's summer, after all!</i>

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.870
You there! Run!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.460
You should be running on 
a gentle slope like this!

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.840
<i>I thought she said "mountain climbing"!</i>

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.050
<i>This is straight-up mountain running!</i>

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.220
What the heck is all this?

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.470
No wonder the Fujisaki players 
are built so strong.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.300
H-Huh?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:12.180
This doesn't seem to be 
bothering Mashima at all...

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.350
Curse him!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:16.560
Curse him for being a former soccer player!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:21.730
We only have until the evening today,
so you'll be playing four matches.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.490
I've prepared a match lineup. It'll be
posted with your first three match-ups.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.820
Your results in those three will
decide your opponent for the fourth.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.460
Sit at the number assigned to you.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.080
<i>Oh, my first match is with Yama-chan.</i>

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.580
<b>Second Match (13:00) 
1 Ayase vs. Yamashiro</b>

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.080
<b>Third Match (14:30) 
Ayase vs. Yamashiro</b>

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.590
<b>Dunnn</b>

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.590
<i>Ayase versus Yamashiro for three matches?!</i>

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.590
<i>No... I can't make it through 
three matches with Ayase-san!</i>

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.590
<i>My knees are already aching...</i>

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.060
Yama-chan! Let's have some good games!

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.770
<i>This is hopeless.
She's already in flight mode.</i>

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:57.900
<b>Tremble Tremble</b>

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.900
<i>But I'm still making you 
play her three times.</i>

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.440
<i>Rion lacks stamina and 
an attachment to karuta.</i>

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:06.900
<i>Even if Ayase-san can only play left-handed,
playing her will be worth it.</i>

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.700
Coach Sakurazawa is amazing, isn't she?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:10.570
Huh?

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:13.330
I mean, having us play each other
three times in a row?

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:16.330
That means we're practicing 
for the Queen match!

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:23.130
<b>Gush</b>

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.040
<i>She's too optimistic!</i>

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.130
<i>She has a permanent hot spring in her heart!</i>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:28.760
I'm not trying to become 
the Queen or anything.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.760
What? But you're so good.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.180
Begin memorization time.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.640
First Match

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:40.440
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.440
<i>When I must hide...</i>

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:48.740
<i>Yama-chan is fast on all 
of my best poems, too.</i>

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.990
<i>Her arm moves in a straight line, and fast.</i>

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.870
<i>My left hand...</i>

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.910
<i>still feels heavy.</i>

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.950
<i>Too slow!</i>

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.460
<i>Yama-chan's arm speed 
will beat mine for sure!</i>

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:01.460
<i>But...</i>

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.670
<i>Rain takes longer...</i>

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:05.590
<i>I have to...</i>

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.550
<i>make this match worthwhile!</i>

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:16.520
<i>leaving a hovering mist 
above the trees and grass</i>

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.810
<i>What does it mean to have good game sense?</i>

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.440
<i>Knowing the sounds leading up
to the first syllable?</i>

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.860
<i>What are we listening for?</i>

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.990
Thank you very much.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:31.610
You have until 1 PM to finish lunch.
The second match will begin right afterward.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.990
<i>I lost big... That was hardly even a game.</i>

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:37.490
<i>But the card differential isn't the point!
What game sense means...</i>

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.880
Ayase-san, you need to eat lunch!

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.920
Ayase-san!

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.820
Mashima-kun, let me take you 
to a great convenience store.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:48.710
Cheers!

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.540
Thanks for waking me up, Yama-chan.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.540
And for sharing your rice balls with me.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:58.590
It's fine. I have plenty of lunch.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.100
Shrimp mayo   Spam   Plum paste & okaka
Beef tongue   Cheese & ground meat   Salmon roe 
Eel   Fried chicken   Tuna & onion

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.100
Beef rib & salty sauce   Meatball 
Bacon   Boiled egg 
Grilled cod roe   Salmon   Wasabi soy sauce

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.390
You're going to eat all those?!

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:03.460
Both levels?!

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:06.290
When you're so skinny? 
And you hate exercising?!

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.370
Rion.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:16.490
<b>Landowner</b>

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.850
You can have some of my rice,

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:18.230
so please continue to play 
karuta in my karuta society.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.240
<b>Rice</b>

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:20.050
Okay, Grandma!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.500
<b>Thanks, Mom...                             Sniffle...</b>

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.500
<b>Heavy</b>

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:24.590
Y-You kept playing karuta for the rice?

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:27.280
In my family, rice problems are a big deal.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:29.380
<b>Rice Specialist</b>

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.390
I don't care about being the Queen.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.720
But when I came to Fujisaki, I ended up 
becoming the club's vice president.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:40.280
It's on you to make sure that we don't 
lose a single match next summer.

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.230
I won't lose in next year's 
High School Championship.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.290
Yama-chan...

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:58.740
What do you think it means 
to have "good game sense"?

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:05.310
I want to play formidable opponents and win,

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:10.510
but I feel like I'm still just taking cards
 without any rhyme or reason.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.930
I don't know anything about that.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.870
It's 1 PM.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.430
Second Match

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.590
<i>So spring ends...</i>

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:26.820
<i>While it may be...</i>

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.700
<i>The reader isn't very good.</i>

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.810
<i>I can tell it's throwing off
Yama-chan's focus.</i>

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:36.830
<i>Coach Sakurazawa has been deliberately</i>

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.980
<i>picking different types of readers
since yesterday...</i>

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.620
<i>Like a boatsman...</i>

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.670
<i>She keeps getting faster.</i>

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:47.400
<i>She's starting to master 
using her left hand.</i>

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:50.700
<i>But what good will that do?</i>

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:53.330
<i>"Even if I'm hurt, I don't 
want to stop playing karuta!"</i>

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.230
<i>"And if I'm going to play, I want to win!"</i>

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:59.480
<i>How can she be so greedy?</i>

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:01.620
Thank you very much.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:03.970
<i>But I still lost by nine! Crap!</i>

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.480
Third Match

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:15.250
<i>May it be that...</i>

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:19.050
<i>Yikes... I almost bit on a dead card.</i>

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.150
<i>I went where the card was
in the second match.</i>

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.580
<i>The fall paddy shacks...</i>

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:24.990
<i>A fault!</i>

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:29.240
<i>So this is what it's like to play 
the same person three times.</i>

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:33.040
<i>Her card placements are similar,
which confuses my memory.</i>

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.820
<i>I remember the previous match's 
layout and mess up.</i>

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:37.990
<i>I start feeling tired
by the third match, too.</i>

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:42.350
<i>And my knees are killing me
from going after cards.</i>

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:45.920
<i>But I have to focus. Focus!</i>

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:54.070
I never give advice during a match,

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.610
but just one thing...

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:00.380
Maintain your posture.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:04.580
All Masters and Queens throughout history
have had good posture.

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:08.080
They've all had truly beautiful form.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:12.710
Rather than taking cards by speed,
do it with grace in your natural form.

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:16.250
Be able to do that,
no matter how tired you are.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:20.350
Sorry. Go ahead.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:25.930
<i>Coach Sakurazawa used Masters 
and Queens as a reference...</i>

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.680
<i>She's never given any of us
advice like that.</i>

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:32.600
<i>Is it because it's Ayase-san?</i>

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:36.120
<i>Posture...</i>

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:38.920
<i>Of course... My posture!</i>

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:42.590
<i>My back was bent, and that was 
making it hard to breathe.</i>

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:47.130
<i>Stay in my natural form, 
and keep it graceful...</i>

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:54.290
<i>Oh... It's just like Kana-chan always said.</i>

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.430
<i>The sky may hold...</i>

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:00.540
<i>A house left to the weeds...</i>

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.790
<i>I just gave advice about posture, 
and Rion's still so haphazard.</i>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.180
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.570
<i>I'm sure you don't know it yet,</i>

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.790
<i>but the ability to change is an asset.</i>

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.390
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.450
<b>Agonizes over the defeat
with good posture</b>

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:21.680
<i>But I still lost by seven!</i>

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.450
Ugh, three losses in a row

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.610
For me...

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:26.430
It's different when my grandma is reading...

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:29.120
but when regular people are reading,

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:32.360
I think I listen for whether 
the sound is high or low.

00:20:32.570 --> 00:20:33.430
Huh?

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:36.880
The pitch of the sound right 
before the unique syllable...

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:39.440
The... pitch...

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:42.770
<i>When the misty bridge... 
When I must hide...</i>

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:44.210
<i>Would the mountain... Would this old...</i>

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:45.670
<i>Feel sorrow wash... Feel love deepen...</i>

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:47.110
<i>Like the sound... Like a boatsman...</i>

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.160
<i>Since I could not... Since the dew...</i>

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:52.640
<i>There's a difference
when they're read out loud?</i>

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:55.100
<i>I think I can grasp it!</i>

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.640
Check the lineup for the fourth match,
then take your seats.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:02.880
We're behind schedule, so be quick!

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:07.240
Between "As this" and "As I," 
which has a higher pitch, Yama-chan?

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.240
I don't know!

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:09.870
Jeez, I shouldn't have given 
you those rice balls!

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.130
I'm so hungry!

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:11.900
Chihaya.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.750
Oh, Taichi. What's up?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.540
We're playing.

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:19.750
We'll begin as soon as 
that clock hits 4.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:28.300
<i>I think Mashima plays better 
when you're not with him.</i>

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.610
Chihaya, why aren't you sitting down?

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:35.560
I know you're tired.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.820
Hey! Why'd you get up?

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:42.650
I can't sit while a girl is standing.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:45.100
What're you talking about? 
There are tons of empty seats!

00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:46.520
I don't get you!

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:48.570
Just because you won? I don't get you!

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:53.040
<i>Taichi...</i>

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:55.910
<i>was like a different person.</i>

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:01.120
I hope your right hand is better soon.

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:06.960
This fall, I'm gonna beat you playing 
right-handed in an official match.

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.270
Hot!

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:15.820
Coach Sakurazawa,

00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:19.150
why did you put the Mizusawa players
together in the last match?

00:22:19.790 --> 00:22:23.080
They're from the same school,
so they can play each other anytime.

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.860
Mashima-kun won every match 
he played at this camp.

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:27.910
No other players were a match for him.

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:30.840
But Ayase-san was playing left-handed,

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:32.530
and she was really tired...

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:36.830
He seems like he could make vast strides 
with just a little more confidence.

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:38.530
And I think...

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:41.840
there's a kind of confidence 
only Ayase-san can give him.
